[1] (source: voice_call_scripts.md)
Thank you for calling AeroSports Scarborough! How can I help you today? Use a warm, upbeat tone.

One moment while I look that up for you. Use this phrase when retrieving information.

Let me connect you with one of our team members who can help you with that. One moment please. This is used when the question is beyond what the AI can handle.

Thanks for calling AeroSports Scarborough! We look forward to seeing you. Have a great day! Always end on a positive note.

We are located at one thousand one hundred and twenty Birchmount Road in Scarborough. The postal code is M1K 5G4. Speak the address clearly and slowly.

Our operating hours are from ten o'clock in the morning until eight o'clock in the evening, Sunday through Thursday, and from ten o'clock in the morning until ten o'clock in the evening on Friday and Saturday. Say times clearly with AM/PM.

The Premium Jump Pass costs twenty-four dollars and ninety cents for ninety minutes, while the VIP Jump Pass is priced at twenty-nine dollars and ninety cents for one hundred and twenty minutes. We also offer an All Day Pass for thirty-nine dollars and ninety cents and an ultimate pass which includes go karting and laser tag for forty-nine dollars and ninety cents for one hundred and eighty minutes. Please note that all prices are plus tax. Aero Socks, required for participation, cost three dollars and ninety-nine cents but they are reusable so you can bring them back next time.

We have three birthday party packages available. The Premium Party starts at thirty-nine dollars and ninety cents per jumper, offering seventy-five minutes of jump time and forty-five minutes in a private party room. The VIP Party is priced at forty-four dollars and ninety cents per jumper with ninety minutes of jump time and sixty minutes of room time. Lastly, the Ultimate Party costs fifty-nine dollars and ninety cents per jumper, providing one hundred and twenty minutes of jump time, sixty minutes of room time, plus go karting for every jumper. All packages include pizza and drinks, with a minimum requirement of ten jumpers. Would you like more details on any package?

Go karting is available on two tracks at our facility. The main track is suitable for riders who are fifty-four inches or taller and costs nineteen dollars and ninety cents for a standalone race or nine dollars and ninety cents as an add-on if you already have a jump pass. The mini track accommodates riders who are thirty-six inches or taller, with a standalone cost of nine dollars and ninety cents or four dollars and ninety cents as an add-on. Each race allows up to ten laps. Remember that closed-toed shoes are required for go karting.

You can book online at our website aerosportsparks.ca, or I can assist you with the booking process right now. Would you like to proceed?

Everyone who enters the park needs a signed waiver, including non-jumpers. You have the option to fill it out online ahead of time on our website to save time at check-in. For anyone under eighteen years old, a parent or legal guardian must sign the waiver. Emphasize completing the waiver online to reduce wait times.

For groups of fifteen or more people, we offer a twenty-five percent discount with the code GROUPBOOKING25, which brings the price down to approximately twenty-five dollars and forty-seven cents per person for one hundred and twenty minutes including socks. Would you like to book a group visit?

Currently, we have an April Birthday Promotion offering up to one hundred and fifty dollars off birthday parties. Use the code APRILBDAY50 for a discount of fifty dollars on a Premium party, APRILBDAY100 for a hundred-dollar discount on a VIP party, or APRILBDAY150 for a one hundred and fifty-dollar discount on an Ultimate party. To qualify, you need to book by April thirty-first and host the event by September thirtieth.

We offer AeroCamp for children aged four to twelve years old. The full-day camp runs from eight-thirty in the morning until four-thirty in the afternoon at a cost of sixty-nine dollars and ninety cents per day or two hundred and ninety-nine dollars and ninety cents for a full week. We also have half-day options available for thirty-nine dollars and ninety cents. Activities include trampolines, games, challenges, crafts, and group activities.

[2] (source: jump_prices.md)
The Open Jump pass options are available for different age groups and include various features. 

For individuals aged six years or older, the Premium Jump Pass costs twenty-four dollars and ninety cents and lasts ninety minutes. This pass grants access to all attractions except Go Karting, Laser tag, Bazooka ball, and Mini golf.

 Alternatively, the VIP Jump Pass for the same age group is priced at twenty-nine dollars and ninety cents and provides one hundred and twenty minutes of access with the same exclusions.

For children aged two to five years, the Premium Jump Pass also costs twenty-four dollars and ninety cents and lasts ninety minutes, offering similar access as the adult version. The VIP Jump Pass for this age group is priced at twenty-nine dollars and ninety cents and provides one hundred and twenty minutes of access with the same exclusions.

For individuals aged six years or older, there is an Ultimate Jump Pass available for forty-nine dollars and ninety cents, which lasts one hundred and eighty minutes. This pass includes access to all core attractions, allowing the choice between Go Karting or Mini golf and Laser tag or Bazooka ball.

Children under two years old can use any pass for free, but a paying adult must accompany them, sharing the same duration as the accompanying parent's pass.

The All Day Pass is available for all ages at thirty-nine dollars and ninety cents, offering unlimited access to attractions throughout the entire day.

Regarding required gear, Aero Socks are priced at three dollars and ninety-nine cents. These socks are reusable and mandatory for all jumpers on all park attractions. Visitors are encouraged to bring them back for future visits.


